Package: BBMF
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Boolean Matrix Factorization
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person(
      given = "Adolphus",
      family = "Wagala",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      email = "adolphus@ds.dfci.harvard.edu"
    )
Description:
    Implements Bayesian Boolean matrix factorization methods for binary
    data developed in "A Bayesian Boolean Matrix Factorization with
    Application to Copy Number Analysis in Cancer" by Wagala, Samur,
    and Parmigiani. The package provides sparse Bayesian Boolean matrix
    factorization, posterior inference using Markov chain Monte Carlo,
    Boolean reconstruction, latent-factor alignment, factor-recovery
    assessment, posterior uncertainty quantification, reconstruction
    diagnostics, and visualization tools. The methodology was motivated
    by the analysis of chromosomal copy number alterations in cancer but
    is applicable to binary matrix data more generally.
